---
args: {"session": "DatasetAuditSession", "edition": "DatasetEditionState | null"}
returns: "DatasetEditionReview"
---
1. Bind prior to edition or DatasetEditionState { revision: 0, use: null, labels: [], families: [], eligibility: [], accounting: [], editions: [], removals: [] }. Inspect changed source events for an authorized consent withdrawal. If present, or if any prior removal still has unresolved lineage or required receipt work, bind removals = traceConsentWithdrawal(session.sourceEvents, prior). Bind heldEdition to prior with the actual new removal cases merged once and revision advanced only for new facts. Return DatasetEditionReview { edition: heldEdition, outcome: "withdrawal-open", proposedRelease: null, acquisitionBriefs: [], ownerQuestions: missing lineage, permission and receipt questions from removals, limitations: the affected derivative/recipient boundaries } before any prospective release. Keep missing lineage and missing delivery receipts visible.
2. Bind use = interpretDatasetUse(session). Treat session.proposedUse as a supplied prior contract to reassess, not an already proven current authorization. Bind labels = establishObservableLabels(use, session.sourceEvents, session.suppliedRules). If a label requires unavailable facts, bind revisedTaskEdition to prior with this use and labels, preserving all family, eligibility, release and removal history. Return DatasetEditionReview { edition: revisedTaskEdition, outcome: "revise-task", proposedRelease: null, acquisitionBriefs: the actual missing label observations, ownerQuestions: unresolved task/permission scope, limitations: unsupported labels }. Do not infer a label from stereotypes or proxy attributes.
3. Bind activeCandidates to supplied candidates outside every still-effective withdrawal and its attributed descendant closure recorded in prior.removals. An incomplete removal receipt never restores use permission. Bind families = buildSourceFamilies(activeCandidates, session.sourceEvents, prior.families). Keep copies, underlying worlds and disputed identity links explicit. Then bind eligibility = adjudicateRecordUse(activeCandidates, use, families, session).
4. Bind accounting = accountIndependentCoverage(eligibility, families, use). Count record coverage and independent family coverage separately. A target met through copied examples remains a mechanism or independence gap.
5. Bind release = freezePermittedEdition(use, labels, families, eligibility, accounting, session, prior). Select outcome review-release only for a concrete artifact inventory with closed split groups, audience-specific permissions, supported required slices and exact owner approval. Otherwise select acquire-evidence with targeted acquisition briefs and known limits; assemble the complete state and return in step 6.
6. Bind nextEdition as DatasetEditionState { revision: advance only for changed source decisions, use, labels, families, eligibility, accounting, editions: prior.editions plus the concrete returned release once when non-null, removals: prior.removals }. Preserve historical releases and their permission bindings. Return DatasetEditionReview { edition: nextEdition, outcome: "review-release" only for the supported concrete release otherwise "acquire-evidence", proposedRelease: release, acquisitionBriefs: specific unsupported slices/labels/artifacts and their acquisition work, ownerQuestions: unresolved permission or exact approval questions, limitations: unresolved identity, independence and coverage limits }. This returns proposed state for an approved host commit; no text claims actual release or removal without its artifact and receiver receipts.
